<title>CANADA: Ag Canada sets February grain Supply/Disposition.</title>
<headline>Ag Canada sets February grain Supply/Disposition.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agriculture Canada Monday set</p>
<p>its February forecast of supply and disposition of grains and</p>
<p>oilseeds in crop year 1996/97 (Aug/July) and 1997/98.</p>
<p>CROP/YR  HARVESTED YIELD OUTPUT SUPPLY EXPORTS CARRYOUT PRICE</p>
<p>DURUM   ('000 ha) (t/ha)     -- '000 of tonnes --	 (C$/t)</p>
<p>1995/96  2,125     2.188 4,648  6,116  3,222   2,023    286</p>
<p>1996/97  2,096     2.243 4,703  6,731  3,850   2,000   208-228</p>
<p>1997/98  2,178     2.222 4,840  6,845  3,900   2,100   185-215</p>
<p>WHEAT EX-DURUM</p>
<p>1995/96  9,017    2.259 20,369 24,601 12,977   4,610    254</p>
<p>1996/97 10,556    2.443 25,792 30,503 16,000   7,100   195-215</p>
<p>1997/98 10,080    2.343 23,620 30,740 17,500   6,000   160-190</p>
<p>ALL WHEAT</p>
<p>1995/96 11,141    2.245 25,017 30,717 16,198   6,633     ---</p>
<p>1996/97 12,652    2.410 30,495 37,233 19,850   9,100     ---</p>
<p>1997/98 12,258    2.322 28,460 37,585 21,400   8,100     ---</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p>1995/96  4,365    2.986 13,035 14,866  2,826   1,807    170</p>
<p>1996/97  4,928    3.229 15,912 17,729  4,000   3,200   125-145</p>
<p>1997/98  4,341    3.110 13,500 16,710  3,800   2,100   110-140</p>
<p>CANOLA</p>
<p>1995/96  5,273    1.221  6,436  7,123  2,804     925    433</p>
<p>1996/97  3,479    1.448  5,037  6,027  2,375     505   430-460</p>
<p>1997/98  5,079    1.324  6,725  7,260  2,850     610   390-430</p>
<p>FLAXSEED</p>
<p>1995/96    860    1.285  1,105  1,207    842     172    342</p>
<p>1996/97    590    1.458    860  1,033    700     125   360-390</p>
<p>1997/98    785    1.357  1,065  1,191    800     171   320-360</p>
<p>SOYBEANS</p>
